          "thread": "MEV and oracle extractable value",
          "why": "The Prisma/Curve analysis quantifying bot-extracted MEV from oracle updates, paired with UMA's Oval product designed to recapture that value for protocols, pulled readers who see oracle tick timing as a profit center — not just a price feed."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Oracle-free lending alternatives",
          "why": "BAMM's AMM-native lending and Frankencoin's oracle-free stablecoin attracted readers looking for DeFi designs that eliminate oracle dependency as a systemic attack surface altogether."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Oracle misconfiguration exploits",
          "why": "A cluster of incidents — Moonwell rsETH feed manipulation, Ribbon Finance, Rho Market's whitehat, Hyperliquid's TVL-based oracle, Peapods Finance, Asymmetry's tBTC halt — showed readers that most oracle exploits are configuration failures, not protocol breaks, making them feel preventable and therefore frustrating."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Decentralized oracle network launches",
          "why": "Chaos Labs Edge ($30B stealth volume), Chronicle's RWA oracle, and RedStone's Credora acquisition all landed in clicks, reflecting reader appetite for challengers to Chainlink rather than coverage of Chainlink itself."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "Prediction market oracle stacks",
          "why": "Truemarkets and the UMA x Polymarket x EigenLayer combination drew readers specifically interested in dispute-resolution oracle design — a niche that sits at the intersection of oracle infrastructure and prediction market credibility."
        },
        {
          "source": "",
          "thread": "TradFi oracle integration milestones",
          "why": "Chainlink's DTCC/Swift/Euroclear pilot achieving 100% data consensus attracted readers tracking how oracle networks are being positioned as the connective tissue for institutional tokenization."
        }
